Chapter: ChainedArrowType

 A chained '->' in a type (A -> B -> C) is rejected; multi-parameter
 types must use commas (A, B -> C). The two forms parsed to the same
 AST, so the arrow chain was a redundant spelling.

Section: Definitions

  add : Integer -> Integer -> Integer
  add (x) (y) = x + y

  opening : Integer = add 2 3

